---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const sections = [
	{ id: 'website-analytics', label: 'Website analytics' },
	{ id: 'enquiries-and-bookings', label: 'Enquiries and bookings' },
	{ id: 'client-records', label: 'Client records' },
	{ id: 'confidentiality-and-its-limits', label: 'Confidentiality and its limits' },
	{ id: 'data-breaches', label: 'Data breaches' },
	{ id: 'your-rights', label: 'Your rights' },
	{ id: 'third-party-services', label: 'Third-party services' },
	{ id: 'questions', label: 'Questions' },
];
---

<Layout
	title="Privacy & Confidentiality"
	description="How this practice handles website analytics, enquiry information, and client records."
	noindex
>
	<article class="privacy-page">
		<div class="wrap">
			<a class="back-link" href="/">← Home</a>
			<h1>Privacy &amp; Confidentiality</h1>

			<p class="intro">
				I take privacy seriously, both as a general obligation to anyone visiting this website and as a
				core part of how I practise as a counsellor. This page explains what information I collect, how I
				use and store it, and what confidentiality means in the context of counselling specifically —
				including its limits. The confidentiality and record-keeping practices described here follow the
				Australian Counselling Association (ACA) Code of Ethics and Practice, which I'm registered under,
				and reflect comparable standards set out in the PACFA Code of Ethics and PACFA's Guidelines on
				Client Records.
			</p>

			<nav class="jump-nav" aria-label="Page sections">
				<span class="jump-nav-label">Jump to:</span>
				{
					sections.map((section, i) => (
						<>
							{i > 0 && <span class="jump-nav-sep">·</span>}
							<a href={`#${section.id}`}>{section.label}</a>
						</>
					))
				}
			</nav>

			<div class="prose">
				<section id="website-analytics">
					<h2>Website analytics</h2>
					<p>
						This site uses a lightweight, privacy-focused analytics tool (GoatCounter) to understand
						how many people visit, which pages they read, and what they've clicked. This tool doesn't
						use cookies, doesn't track you across other websites, and doesn't collect anything that
						identifies you personally. It gives me aggregate numbers only — how many visits, from
						roughly where, and which pages get read — not who visited.
					</p>
				</section>

				<hr />

				<section id="enquiries-and-bookings">
					<h2>Enquiries and bookings</h2>
					<p>
						If you get in touch through the contact form or booking system, I collect what you provide,
						typically your name, contact details, and anything you write in your message. This is used
						only to respond to you and, if you go ahead, to arrange and manage sessions. It isn't
						shared with third parties beyond the booking software itself, and isn't used for marketing.
					</p>
				</section>

				<hr />

				<section id="client-records">
					<h2>Client records (session notes)</h2>
					<p>
						If you become a client, I keep clinical records of our work together. This is both a
						professional requirement and good practice — it helps me provide continuity of care and is
						expected under the ACA Code of Ethics and Practice, which requires client records to be
						kept securely, whether in digital or hard-copy form.
					</p>
					<p>
						<strong>What I keep:</strong> brief session notes covering what we discussed, clinical
						observations, and any plans or referrals. I don't record sessions or keep verbatim
						transcripts.
					</p>
					<p>
						<strong>How it's stored:</strong> records are kept in a secure, access-controlled system,
						separate from general business records. Only I have access to them.
					</p>
					<p>
						<strong>How long I keep them:</strong> in line with standard practice for health records in
						Australia, adult client records are retained for at least 7 years after the last contact.
						Records for clients who were minors at the time of counselling are retained until they
						turn 25. After that period, records are securely destroyed.
					</p>
				</section>

				<hr />

				<section id="confidentiality-and-its-limits">
					<h2>Confidentiality — and its limits</h2>
					<p>
						Everything discussed in sessions is confidential. I don't share the content of our
						conversations with anyone else, including family members, without your consent, except in
						the following circumstances:
					</p>
					<ul>
						<li>
							<strong>Risk of serious harm.</strong> If I believe there's a serious risk to your life
							or safety, or to someone else's, I may need to act to prevent that harm, which can
							include contacting emergency services or another relevant party.
						</li>
						<li>
							<strong>Mandatory reporting.</strong> Counsellors in the ACT are subject to mandatory
							reporting obligations regarding the safety of children. If information raises a
							mandatory reporting concern, I'm legally required to act on it.
						</li>
						<li>
							<strong>Legal requirement.</strong> If a court orders disclosure of records (for
							example, via subpoena), I may be legally required to comply, though I'll do what I
							reasonably can to protect your privacy within that process.
						</li>
						<li>
							<strong>Clinical supervision.</strong> I discuss aspects of my work in professional
							supervision, as required by the ACA, but this is done in a way that protects your
							identity wherever possible.
						</li>
					</ul>
					<p>
						Sessions themselves are private — they won't be recorded, overheard, or observed by anyone
						else without your informed consent, in line with ACA standards on session privacy.
					</p>
					<p>
						The ACA requires these terms, and the degree of confidentiality offered, to be agreed with
						you clearly before counselling begins — so I'll always talk this through with you directly
						at the start of our work together, not just leave it on a page.
					</p>
				</section>

				<hr />

				<section id="data-breaches">
					<h2>Data breaches</h2>
					<p>
						In the unlikely event of a data breach involving your personal information that's likely to
						result in serious harm, I'll notify you and the Office of the Australian Information
						Commissioner (OAIC), in line with the Notifiable Data Breaches scheme.
					</p>
				</section>

				<hr />

				<section id="your-rights">
					<h2>Your rights</h2>
					<p>
						You can ask to see the personal information I hold about you, ask me to correct it if it's
						wrong, and ask questions about how it's handled at any time. If you have a concern about
						how your information has been handled, you're welcome to raise it with me directly first.
						If it's not resolved to your satisfaction, you can make a complaint to:
					</p>
					<ul>
						<li>
							ACA (as my professional association) —{' '}
							<a href="https://www.theaca.net.au/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
								theaca.net.au
							</a>
						</li>
						<li>
							The Office of the Australian Information Commissioner (OAIC) —{' '}
							<a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
								oaic.gov.au
							</a>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</section>

				<hr />

				<section id="third-party-services">
					<h2>Third-party services this site uses</h2>
					<ul>
						<li>GoatCounter — anonymous website analytics</li>
						<li>
							<em>[Booking/practice management software — name once chosen]</em> — for scheduling and
							client records
						</li>
						<li>
							<em>[Email provider, e.g. Fastmail]</em> — for professional correspondence
						</li>
					</ul>
				</section>

				<hr />

				<section id="questions">
					<h2>Questions</h2>
					<p>
						If you have any questions about this policy or how your information is handled, contact me
						at <a class="value" id="privacy-email-link" href="#">this email</a>.
					</p>
				</section>
			</div>

			<p class="meta-footer">Last updated: <em>[date pending]</em>.</p>
		</div>
	</article>
</Layout>

<script>
	const link = document.getElementById('privacy-email-link');
	if (link instanceof HTMLAnchorElement) {
		const address = atob('aGVsbG9AYmVubWFjbGFyZW4uY29tLmF1');
		link.href = `mailto:${address}`;
		link.textContent = address;
	}
</script>

<style>
	.privacy-page {
		padding: var(--space-15) 0 var(--space-20);
	}

	.back-link {
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: var(--fs-caption);
		letter-spacing: var(--ls-label);
		text-transform: uppercase;
		text-decoration: none;
		color: var(--color-text-secondary);
		display: inline-block;
		margin-bottom: var(--space-10);
	}

	.back-link:hover {
		color: var(--color-accent);
	}

	h1 {
		font-size: var(--fs-display);
		line-height: var(--lh-article-title);
		max-width: 70ch;
		margin-bottom: var(--space-5);
	}

	.intro {
		font-size: var(--fs-prose-body);
		color: var(--color-text-secondary);
		max-width: 70ch;
		margin: 0 0 var(--space-8);
	}

	.jump-nav {
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: var(--fs-caption);
		color: var(--color-text-secondary);
		max-width: 70ch;
		margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
		line-height: var(--lh-loose);
	}

	.jump-nav-label {
		color: var(--color-text-muted);
		margin-right: var(--space-1);
	}

	.jump-nav a {
		color: var(--color-text-secondary);
		text-decoration: underline;
		text-underline-offset: 2px;
	}

	.jump-nav a:hover {
		color: var(--color-accent);
	}

	.jump-nav-sep {
		color: var(--color-text-muted);
		margin: 0 var(--space-1);
	}

	.prose {
		max-width: 70ch;
		font-size: var(--fs-prose-body);
		color: var(--color-text-secondary);
	}

	.prose h2 {
		font-size: var(--fs-h1);
		color: var(--color-text-primary);
		margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
		scroll-margin-top: var(--space-8);
	}

	.prose p {
		margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
	}

	.prose p:last-child {
		margin-bottom: 0;
	}

	.prose strong {
		color: var(--color-text-primary);
	}

	.prose ul {
		margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
		padding-left: var(--space-5);
	}

	.prose ul:last-child {
		margin-bottom: 0;
	}

	.prose li {
		margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
	}

	.prose li:last-child {
		margin-bottom: 0;
	}

	.prose a {
		color: var(--color-accent-link);
		text-decoration: underline;
	}

	.prose a:hover {
		color: var(--color-accent);
	}

	.prose section {
		padding: var(--space-8) 0;
	}

	.prose section:first-child {
		padding-top: 0;
	}

	.prose hr {
		border: none;
		border-top: var(--border-hairline) solid var(--color-border);
		margin: 0;
	}

	.meta-footer {
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: var(--fs-meta-label);
		color: var(--color-text-muted);
		max-width: 70ch;
		margin-top: var(--space-12);
		padding-top: var(--space-8);
		border-top: var(--border-hairline) solid var(--color-border);
	}
</style>
